$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/capability-token
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  The capability token is the only secret-bearing artefact an agent reasons about. A short-lived,
  scoped, audience-bound handle that contains zero secret material, it is safe to pass through
  prompts, memory, tool calls, and multi-agent buses where a value is not.
$system: smith-gray/system
$service: smith-gray/control-plane
status: planned
intent: |
  Agents must be able to define, create, transport, and request use of secrets without ever
  receiving plaintext or long-term keys. A token decouples "the right to use a secret" from "the
  secret" itself, so authority can travel through untrusted channels — model context, logs, MCP
  buses — while the value cannot.

flows:
  - id: mint-token
    name: Mint a capability token
    description: The control plane issues a signed token for a specific object, scope, and audience.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: receive
        target: Control plane receives an object id, requested scope, audience, and TTL from the sidecar.
      - id: s2
        action: validate
        target: Policy is evaluated — is this requester allowed to mint this scope for this object and audience?
      - id: s3
        action: generate
        target: Generate claims (sid, scope, aud, exp, nbf, jti) and sign with the active kid.
      - id: s4
        action: record
        target: Persist the jti so it can be revoked and audited.
      - id: s5
        action: receive
        target: Caller receives the token URI; no secret material is present in the response.
  - id: verify-token
    name: Verify a token at the sidecar
    description: The sidecar is the only component that validates a token before resolving.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: parse
        target: Parse the safekey:// URI and extract the token and claims.
      - id: s2
        action: validate
        target: Verify signature against the issuer's key (kid), then expiry (exp/nbf).
      - id: s3
        action: validate
        target: Verify the audience matches this resolver/environment identity.
      - id: s4
        action: validate
        target: Verify the requested operation is within the token's scope (least privilege).
      - id: s5
        action: validate
        target: Check the jti against the revocation denylist.
      - id: s6
        action: observe
        target: On any failure, deny by default without revealing why beyond a generic denial code.

contracts:
  - id: token-contains-no-secrets
    description: A capability token must never contain plaintext, key material, or anything that yields it.
    must_have:
      - Claims are limited to object identifier, scope, audience, time bounds, unique id, and signature
      - No field may carry the secret value, a DEK, or a KEK
      - A token captured from a prompt or log is not sufficient to decrypt a folder without a reachable sidecar and key authority
  - id: short-lived-and-scoped
    description: Tokens are least-privilege and short-lived by construction.
    must_have:
      - TTL measured in minutes to hours, never days
      - scope is one of read, unwrap, inject-env, inject-file, sign
      - aud binds the token to an intended resolver identity or environment
  - id: revocable
    description: Every token can be invalidated immediately, independent of its TTL.
    must_have:
      - A unique jti is issued and recorded at mint time
      - Revocation is enforced by a denylist checked on every resolve
      - Revocation takes effect without waiting for expiry
  - id: signature-verifiable
    description: The sidecar can verify authenticity offline of the issuing control plane's authority.
    must_have:
      - Tokens are signed and carry a key id
      - Signature verification happens before any key-store interaction
      - An unverifiable token is denied

tests:
  - id: token-has-no-secret-material
    flow: mint-token
    setup:
      secret_value: "super-secret-value"
    expect:
      - assertion: the minted token string does not contain the secret value in any encoding
      - assertion: decoding the token yields only the declared claims
      - assertion: no DEK or KEK identifier resolves to recoverable key bytes
    contracts:
      - token-contains-no-secrets
  - id: expired-token-denied
    flow: verify-token
    setup:
      ttl_seconds: 1
      wait_seconds: 2
    expect:
      - assertion: resolution is denied with a generic denial
      - assertion: no key-store unwrap is attempted
    contracts:
      - short-lived-and-scoped
  - id: wrong-audience-denied
    flow: verify-token
    setup:
      aud: "env-production"
      resolver_identity: "env-staging"
    expect:
      - assertion: resolution is denied
      - assertion: no plaintext is materialised
    contracts:
      - short-lived-and-scoped
  - id: revoked-token-denied-immediately
    flow: verify-token
    setup:
      revoke_before_use: true
      ttl_seconds: 3600
    expect:
      - assertion: resolution is denied even though the token has not expired
    contracts:
      - revocable

decisions:
  - id: uri-form
    decision: "Express tokens as a URI: safekey://v1/<id>?scope=<action>&aud=<env>&exp=<unix>&kid=<key-id>"
    rationale: A URI is copyable through any transport, self-describing, and easy to redact in logs by matching a prefix. It makes the token obviously a handle rather than a value.
    status: accepted
  - id: short-ttl-over-long-lived
    decision: Use short TTL plus a jti denylist rather than long-lived tokens with periodic rotation.
    rationale: Short TTL bounds the damage window of a leaked token; the denylist provides immediate revocation for the cases where waiting is unacceptable. Together they cover both the common and the urgent case.
    status: accepted
  - id: generic-denials
    decision: Denials return a generic failure rather than the specific violated check.
    rationale: Detailed denial reasons are a probing oracle for an attacker refining a forged token.
    status: accepted

implementation:
  primary: apps/control-plane/internal/token
  test_code: ""
  test_code_status: none

see_also:
  - "smith-gray/secret-transport"
  - "smith-gray/token-revocation"
  - "smith-gray/sidecar-resolution"
